# Line endings.
#
# A Mac refuses a shell file whose lines end the Windows way. The error it gives
# is "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", which says nothing to the person reading it
# and stops the install on its first line. Git was rewriting setup.command to
# Windows endings on the way in, so a Mac member cloning this would have hit
# exactly that. These lines pin the files that must stay as they are.
*.command text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf

# And the Windows installer must keep Windows endings for the same reason in
# reverse - a .cmd file with Unix endings misreads its own labels.
*.cmd     text eol=crlf
